config BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_DISPLAYPORT
	bool "cadr-displayport"
	# Depends on cadr-common rather than selecting it, as the board's
	# address map does: the map is a choice inside cadr-common, and a
	# package that selected cadr-common while depending on the map would be
	# a recursive dependency, which Kconfig answers by dropping the map.
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON && BR2_CADR_BOARD_KR260
	help
	  The Kria KR260's DisplayPort link, for the display output in
	  the fabric.  The display output puts the machine's screens on
	  a 1920x1080 raster and hands it to the processing system's
	  DisplayPort controller's live video input; this program sets
	  up the transceiver lane, trains the link with the monitor,
	  tells the controller what the stream is, and follows the
	  display output's sleep: the monitor is told D3 and the stream
	  stops when the display is muted, and D0 and the stream come
	  back when it is let go.  Pixels never pass through it.

	  The Kria KR260's alone, and only with a display output in the
	  fabric: it reads the console's word 36 first, and stops on a
	  fabric whose word carries no display output's marker.

comment "cadr-displayport is the Kria KR260's"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON || !BR2_CADR_BOARD_KR260
